      },
      "body": "Fixes the Intel CI failure in `test_basic_cumem` (intel-ci build 15032): `XpuMemAllocator.sleep()` called `torch.xpu.empty_cache()` directly, so the test's `torch.accelerator.empty_cache` hook saw 0 calls. Now it uses `torch.accelerator.empty_cache()` and synchronizes before unmapping in the free callback, matching the CUDA `CuMemAllocator`.\n\nNot a duplicate: no open PR touches this (searched `xpumem empty_cache`, `test_basic_cumem XPU`).\n\nValidation: root-caused from the CI log; could not run the test locally (local env lacks libcuda for the test import). Needs Intel CI to confirm.\n\nAI assistance (GitHub Copilot) was used; reviewed by the submitter.",
